  view_file {
    absolute_path_uri: "file:///skills/system_skills/gemini_api/references/image_video_music.md"
    end_line: 223
    content: "# Image, Video, and Music Generation (`@google/genai`)\n\n> All `@google/genai` calls below run **server-side** using the shared\n> `GoogleGenAI` client initialized with `process.env.GEMINI_API_KEY` and\n> `\'User-Agent\': \'aistudio-build\'` (see `SKILL.md`).\n\n## Generate Images\n\n### Image Generation and Editing Model\n\n-   Generate images using `gemini-3.1-flash-lite-image` by default.\n-   Upgrade to `gemini-nano-banana-2.1` if the user requests any of the\n    following:\n    -   High-quality images with configurable resolution (1K, 2K, or 4K).\n    -   Non-standard aspect ratios: \"1:4\", \"1:8\", \"4:1\", or \"8:1\".\n    -   Real-time information using the `googleSearch` tool.\n    -   Image search: using web images retrieved via Google Image Search as\n        context for image generation.\n-   The `googleSearch` tool is only available to `gemini-3-pro-image` and\n    `gemini-nano-banana-2.1`; do not use it with `gemini-3.1-flash-lite-image`.\n    Within `googleSearch`, `imageSearch` is only available to\n    `gemini-nano-banana-2.1`.\n-   When using nano banana series models, users **MUST** select their own API\n    key. See the \"Paid API Key\" section in `SKILL.md` for details.\n\n### Image Configuration\n\n-   `aspectRatio`: Changes the aspect ratio of the generated image. Supported\n    values are \"1:1\", \"3:4\", \"4:3\", \"9:16\", and \"16:9\". The default is \"1:1\".\n    `gemini-nano-banana-2.1` and `gemini-3-pro-image` additionally support\n    \"1:4\", \"1:8\", \"4:1\", and \"8:1\".\n-   `imageSize`: Changes the size of the generated image. Available for\n    `gemini-3-pro-image` (supports \"1K\", \"2K\", \"4K\"; default \"1K\") and\n    `gemini-nano-banana-2.1` (supports \"1K\", \"2K\", \"4K\"; default \"1K\").\n-   **DO NOT** set `responseMimeType`. It is not supported for nano banana\n    series models.\n-   **DO NOT** set `responseSchema`. It is not supported for nano banana series\n    models.\n\n### Examples\n\n-   Call `generateContent` to generate images with nano banana series models.\n-   The output response may contain both image and text parts; you must iterate\n    through all parts to find the image part. Do not assume the first part is an\n    image part.\n\n```ts\nimport { GoogleGenAI } from \"@google/genai\";\n\n// ... initialization ...\n\nconst response = await ai.models.generateContent({\n  model: \'gemini-nano-banana-2.1\',\n  contents: {\n    parts: [\n      {\n        text: \'A robot holding a red skateboard.\',\n      },\n    ],\n  },\n  config: {\n    imageConfig: {\n          aspectRatio: \"1:1\",\n          imageSize: \"1K\"\n      },\n    tools: [\n      {\n        // Optional, only for `gemini-3-pro-image` and `gemini-nano-banana-2.1`.\n        googleSearch: {\n          searchTypes: {\n            webSearch: {},\n            imageSearch: {}, // Only available for `gemini-nano-banana-2.1`.\n          }\n        },\n      },\n    ],\n  },\n});\nfor (const part of response.candidates?.[0]?.content?.parts ?? []) {\n  // Find the image part, do not assume it is the first part.\n  if (part.inlineData?.data) {\n    const base64EncodeString: string = part.inlineData.data;\n    const mime = part.inlineData.mimeType ?? \"image/png\";\n    const imageUrl = `data:${mime};base64,${base64EncodeString}`;\n  } else if (part.text) {\n    console.log(part.text);\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### Edit Images\n\n-   To edit images using the model, you can prompt with text, images or a\n    combination of both.\n-   Follow the \"Image Generation and Editing Model\" and \"Image Configuration\"\n    sections defined in the \"Generate Images\" section above.\n\n```ts\nimport { GoogleGenAI } from \"@google/genai\";\n\n// ... initialization ...\n\nconst response = await ai.models.generateContent({\n  model: \'gemini-3.1-flash-lite-image\',\n  contents: {\n    parts: [\n      {\n        inlineData: {\n          data: base64ImageData, // base64 encoded string\n          mimeType: mimeType, // IANA standard MIME type\n        },\n      },\n      {\n        text: \'can you add a llama next to the image\',\n      },\n    ],\n  },\n});\nfor (const part of response.candidates?.[0]?.content?.parts ?? []) {\n  // Find the image part, do not assume it is the first part.\n  if (part.inlineData?.data) {\n    const base64EncodeString: string = part.inlineData.data;\n    const mime = part.inlineData.mimeType ?? \"image/png\";\n    const imageUrl = `data:${mime};base64,${base64EncodeString}`;\n  } else if (part.text) {\n    console.log(part.text);\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## Generate Music\n\nGenerate music from a text prompt, optionally combined with an image. Two models\nare available:\n\n-   `lyria-3-clip-preview` (**Lyria Clip**): Short clips up to 30 seconds.\n-   `lyria-3-pro-preview` (**Lyria Pro**): Full-length tracks.\n\nBoth models use `generateContent` or `generateContentStream` and return audio in\nthe same format:\n\n-   Omit `responseModalities` so the response stream returns both audio\n    (`inlineData`) and generated lyrics/metadata (`text`) parts. (Setting\n    `responseModalities: [\"AUDIO\"]` suppresses lyrics text output.)\n-   Unlike Live and streaming TTS (which return raw PCM requiring\n    `AudioContext`), Lyria models return standard encoded audio (**MP3**,\n    `audio/mpeg` by default) that plays directly in an HTML `<audio>` element.\n-   When using Lyria models, users **MUST** select their own API key. See the\n    \"Paid API Key\" section in `SKILL.md` for details.\n\n### Text-Only Music Generation\n\n```ts\nimport { GoogleGenAI } from \"@google/genai\";\n\n// ... initialization ...\n\nconst response = await ai.models.generateContentStream({\n  // \"lyria-3-clip-preview\" (30s) or \"lyria-3-pro-preview\" (full tracks)\n  model: \"lyria-3-clip-preview\",\n  contents: \"Generate a 30-second cinematic orchestral track.\",\n});\n\nconst audioChunks: Buffer[] = [];\nlet lyrics = \"\";\nlet mimeType = \"audio/mpeg\";\n\nfor await (const chunk of response) {\n  const parts = chunk.candidates?.[0]?.content?.parts;\n  if (!parts) continue;\n  for (const part of parts) {\n    if (part.inlineData?.data) {\n      if (audioChunks.length === 0 && part.inlineData.mimeType) {\n        mimeType = part.inlineData.mimeType;\n      }\n      audioChunks.push(Buffer.from(part.inlineData.data, \"base64\"));\n    }\n    if (part.text) {\n      lyrics += part.text;\n    }\n  }\n}\n\nconst audioBase64 = Buffer.concat(audioChunks).toString(\"base64\");\n// Return { audioDataUrl, lyrics } from your server route to the client `<audio>` tag:\nconst audioDataUrl = `data:${mimeType};base64,${audioBase64}`;\n```\n\n### Image + Text Music Generation\n\n```ts\nimport { GoogleGenAI } from \"@google/genai\";\n\n// ... initialization ...\n\nconst response = await ai.models.generateContentStream({\n  // \"lyria-3-clip-preview\" (30s) or \"lyria-3-pro-preview\" (full tracks)\n  model: \"lyria-3-clip-preview\",\n  contents: {\n    parts: [\n      { text: \"Generate a 30-second track inspired by this image.\" },\n      { inlineData: { data: base64ImageData, mimeType: \"image/jpeg\" } },\n    ],\n  },\n});\n\n// Process the stream identically to the text-only example above.\n```\n\n## Video Generation, Editing, and Extension (Omni Flash)\n\nVideo generation, editing, and extension uses the `gemini-omni-1.2-flash` model,\nwhich is **only** supported via the Gemini Interactions API\n(`ai.interactions.create`) and cannot be called with `ai.models.generateContent`\nor `ai.models.generateVideos`.\n\nTo implement video generation, animation, extension, or editing, you **MUST**\nload and follow the **`gemini-interactions-api`** skill by calling `view_file`\non `/skills/system_skills/gemini_interactions_api/SKILL.md` (for its\n**Prerequisites** and **Calling Gemini Interactions API** sections) and\n`/skills/system_skills/gemini_interactions_api/references/image_video_music.md`\n(for its **Video Generation, Editing, and Extension (Omni Flash)** section and\ncode examples).\n"
    num_lines: 224
    num_bytes: 7663
    line_range_bytes: 7663
  }
}
