  view_file {
    absolute_path_uri: "file:///skills/system_skills/gemini_api/references/speech_and_audio.md"
    end_line: 214
    content: "# Speech Generation (TTS) and Audio Transcription (`@google/genai`)\n\n> All `@google/genai` calls below run **server-side** using the shared\n> `GoogleGenAI` client initialized with `process.env.GEMINI_API_KEY` and\n> `\'User-Agent\': \'aistudio-build\'` (see `SKILL.md`).\n\n## Transcribe Audio\n\nUse `gemini-3.5-transcribe` to transcribe pre-recorded or uploaded audio files\ninto text using `generateContent` or `generateContentStream`.\n\n```ts\nimport { GoogleGenAI } from \"@google/genai\";\n\n// ... initialization ...\n\nconst audioPart = {\n  inlineData: {\n    mimeType: \"audio/mp3\", // e.g. \"audio/mp3\", \"audio/wav\", \"audio/webm\"\n    data: base64AudioString,\n  },\n};\n\nconst response = await ai.models.generateContent({\n  model: \"gemini-3.5-transcribe\",\n  contents: { parts: [audioPart, { text: \"Transcribe this audio.\" }] },\n});\n\nconsole.log(response.text);\n```\n\n## Generate Speech\n\nTransform text input into single-speaker or multi-speaker audio. Two models are\navailable (requires `@google/genai` `>= 2.25.0` for `speechMetadata` support;\nrun `npm i @google/genai@latest` if `package.json` has an older version):\n\n-   `gemini-3.8-flash-lite-tts`: High-efficiency, low-latency, cost-optimized\n    audio model. Use by default for general TTS applications, including article\n    reading, global dubbing/localization, customer service IVR, accessibility\n    screen readers, and high-throughput voice assistants.\n-   `gemini-3.8-flash-tts`: Flagship audio model. Reserved for **Voice Design\n    and creation** (prompting custom voice personas from scratch),\n    **dual-speaker screenplay editing**, and **podcasting/dialogue apps\n    requiring backchanneling** (`|mhm|`, `|yeah|`) and scripted vocal bursts\n    (`<laugh>`, `<gasp>`, `<breath>`).\n\n> [!IMPORTANT] **Audio output format (Gemini 3.8 TTS defaults)**:\n>\n> -   **Unary** (`generateContent`): `inlineData.data` is a complete **WAV\n>     file** (`audio/wav`, 44-byte RIFF header, 24kHz, mono, 16-bit). Save the\n>     decoded bytes directly as `.wav` or play them in the browser via `<audio>`\n>     / `Blob` (`type: \"audio/wav\"`). Do **NOT** add a WAV header or decode it\n>     as raw PCM.\n> -   **Streaming** (`generateContentStream`): each chunk\'s `inlineData.data` is\n>     **headerless raw PCM** (`audio/l16`, 24kHz, mono, 16-bit little-endian).\n>     Concatenate the chunks or play them progressively via `AudioContext`\n>     (Int16 \342\206\222 Float32).\n> -   To concatenate multiple unary clips into one file, strip the 44-byte WAV\n>     header from every clip after the first (or use streaming to get raw PCM).\n\n### Single speaker (Standard TTS with `gemini-3.8-flash-lite-tts`)\n\n```ts\nimport { GoogleGenAI } from \"@google/genai\";\n\n// ... initialization ...\n\nconst response = await ai.models.generateContent({\n  model: \"gemini-3.8-flash-lite-tts\",\n  contents: [\n    {\n      role: \"user\",\n      parts: [\n        {\n          text: \"Here is the latest breaking news summary for today.\",\n          speechMetadata: {\n            style: \"Clear, professional news anchor\",\n          },\n        },\n      ],\n    },\n  ],\n  config: {\n    responseModalities: [\"AUDIO\"],\n    speechConfig: {\n      voiceConfig: {\n        // \'Puck\', \'Charon\', \'Kore\', \'Fenrir\', \'Zephyr\'\n        prebuiltVoiceConfig: { voiceName: \"Kore\" },\n      },\n    },\n  },\n});\n\n// Unary default: a complete WAV file (audio/wav, RIFF header, 24kHz mono\n// 16-bit). No header wrapping or PCM decoding needed.\nconst base64Audio =\n  response.candidates?.[0]?.content?.parts?.[0]?.inlineData?.data;\nif (base64Audio) {\n  const wavBuffer = Buffer.from(base64Audio, \"base64\");\n  // ... save as .wav, or return base64 to the client and play it via\n  // new Audio(`data:audio/wav;base64,${base64Audio}`) ...\n}\n```\n\n### Streaming TTS (raw PCM chunks)\n\nUse `generateContentStream` with the same config to receive audio incrementally.\nEach chunk is **headerless raw PCM** (`audio/l16`, 24kHz, mono, 16-bit\nlittle-endian):\n\n```ts\nimport { GoogleGenAI } from \"@google/genai\";\n\n// ... initialization ...\n\nconst responseStream = await ai.models.generateContentStream({\n  model: \"gemini-3.8-flash-lite-tts\",\n  contents: [\n    {\n      role: \"user\",\n      parts: [{ text: \"Say cheerfully: Have a wonderful day!\" }],\n    },\n  ],\n  config: {\n    responseModalities: [\"AUDIO\"],\n    speechConfig: {\n      voiceConfig: {\n        prebuiltVoiceConfig: { voiceName: \"Kore\" },\n      },\n    },\n  },\n});\n\nconst pcmChunks: Buffer[] = [];\nfor await (const chunk of responseStream) {\n  const data = chunk.candidates?.[0]?.content?.parts?.[0]?.inlineData?.data;\n  if (data) {\n    // Raw L16 PCM chunk (24kHz, mono, 16-bit LE). Forward it to the client\n    // (e.g. via SSE/WebSocket) for progressive AudioContext playback, or\n    // collect it.\n    pcmChunks.push(Buffer.from(data, \"base64\"));\n  }\n}\n// Concatenated chunks form one continuous raw PCM stream (no WAV header).\nconst pcm = Buffer.concat(pcmChunks);\n```\n\n### Multi-speakers, Voice Design & Backchanneling (`gemini-3.8-flash-tts`)\n\nUse `gemini-3.8-flash-tts` when you need Voice Design, dual-speaker screenplay\ndirection, or natural podcast dialogue with backchanneling (`|yeah|`, `|mhm|`)\nand vocal bursts (`<breath>`, `<laugh>`, `<gasp>`). When using\n`multiSpeakerVoiceConfig`, the number of `speakerVoiceConfigs` must equal 2.\n\n```ts\nimport { GoogleGenAI } from \"@google/genai\";\n\n// ... initialization ...\n\nconst response = await ai.models.generateContent({\n  model: \"gemini-3.8-flash-tts\",\n  contents: [\n    {\n      role: \"user\",\n      parts: [\n        {\n          text: \"Alex: Welcome back! <breath> Today we are diving deep into AI models.\",\n          speechMetadata: {\n            speaker: \"Alex\",\n            style: \"Enthusiastic, bright podcast host\",\n          },\n        },\n        {\n          text: \"Sam: That\'s right, |yeah| it has been a huge week for speech generation.\",\n          speechMetadata: {\n            speaker: \"Sam\",\n            style: \"Curious, articulate co-host\",\n          },\n        },\n      ],\n    },\n  ],\n  config: {\n    responseModalities: [\"AUDIO\"],\n    speechConfig: {\n      multiSpeakerVoiceConfig: {\n        speakerVoiceConfigs: [\n          {\n            speaker: \"Alex\",\n            voiceConfig: {\n              prebuiltVoiceConfig: { voiceName: \"Puck\" },\n            },\n          },\n          {\n            speaker: \"Sam\",\n            voiceConfig: {\n              prebuiltVoiceConfig: { voiceName: \"Kore\" },\n            },\n          },\n        ],\n      },\n    },\n  },\n});\n\n// Unary default: a complete WAV file (audio/wav, 24kHz mono 16-bit).\nconst base64Audio =\n  response.candidates?.[0]?.content?.parts?.[0]?.inlineData?.data;\nif (base64Audio) {\n  const wavBuffer = Buffer.from(base64Audio, \"base64\");\n  // ... save as .wav, or return base64 to the client for direct playback ...\n}\n```\n"
    num_lines: 215
    num_bytes: 6754
    line_range_bytes: 6754
  }
}
