    thinking: "**Analyzing API Needs**\n\nI\'ve been examining the `gemini-api` skill\'s prerequisites. I\'ve noted that certain models like `gemini-3-pro-image-preview`, `gemini-3-pro-image`, `gemini-4-carbon`, and `gemini-4-argon` all demand a paid API key. My current task is to ensure the user is prompted appropriately to choose one of these if needed.\n\n\n**Prioritizing UI Flow**\n\nI\'ve decided that calling `show_aistudio_ui` with `ui_type: \"paid_model_flow\"` is the immediate next step. This is because the tool description explicitly states that the conversation flow pauses to await user input. There is no need for installing `@google/genai` library first. The critical path is ensuring the user gets the chance to choose a paid key or skip the paid model flow, before any expensive API calls occur. I am now double-checking if the `paid_model_flow` argument needs any further adjustments.\n\n\n**Refining Flow Sequence**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the cleanest execution path. The `SKILL.md` guidance clearly dictates prompting the user *before* model usage. So, `show_aistudio_ui` with `ui_type: \"paid_model_flow\"` is the immediate call. I\'ve re-examined the parameters. The `install_applet_package` for `@google/genai@latest` can be deferred until after the user interaction; keeping the flow clean and prompt is the immediate goal. The \"stop and wait\" requirement of `show_aistudio_ui` confirms this prioritization.\n\n\n**Sequencing the Turn**\n\nI\'m now determining the optimal turn sequence. My current focus is integrating the documentation reading with `show_aistudio_ui`. I will read `references/9_museum_editorial_institutional.md` and then promptly call `show_aistudio_ui`. I will make sure the user\'s turn ends with `show_aistudio_ui`, so we stop and wait.\n\n\n"
