  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Handling API Key Rejection**\n\nI\'ve got it! The user opted out of the paid API key setup, so we\'re sticking with the server-side `process.env.GEMINI_API_KEY`. This means I need to focus on robust error handling for API issues. We should gracefully manage any errors, especially those from paid-tier models like `RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED` or `PERMISSION_DENIED`.\n\n\n**Planning Visual Assets & Packages**\n\nI\'m now focusing on ensuring the right packages are in place, particularly `@google/genai`. I\'ll execute `install_applet_package` with `@google/genai@latest` to meet the version requirements for the specified Gemini models and features. Simultaneously, I\'ll initiate image generation to design visual assets. Thoughtful design of the app is also key.\n\n\n**Defining App Visuals**\n\nI\'m now refining the visual concept, calling it \"Loom & Lantern,\" an illustrated storybook studio for children. I envision a warm, tactile, and legible experience, drawing inspiration from museum and educational references. I\'m focusing on a specific palette with a warm archival paper base, warm sand structural surfaces, and deep cobalt accents. The goal is to avoid generic AI imagery in favor of an authentic and inviting aesthetic.\n\n\n**Refining Color & Typography**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the color palette and typography. I\'ve selected `#C2410C` and `#B45309` for active highlights and controls. For display titles, I\'m going with `Fraunces`, a warm serif, and for body text and UI, `Plus Jakarta Sans`, a clean sans-serif. Both will load directly from Google Fonts. I\'m also planning the top bar layout, ensuring a clear and concise user experience with distinct zones for brand, navigation, and a primary CTA. I\'m structuring a top bar with a strict 1-row, 3-zone layout. The brand will feature \"Loom & Lantern\" in `Fraunces`. Navigation will include four concise links: `Library`, `Read`, `Create Story`, and `Story Buddy`. The final zone will highlight a `New Story` button.\n\n\n**Verifying Build Configurations**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the build and run configurations for the project. I\'m verifying the setup for both \"dev\" and \"start\" scripts, including checking the `tsconfig.json` and assessing the compatibility of `server.ts` with Node 22. My plan is to ensure smooth execution using `tsx` for development and a standard Node environment for production, possibly using type-only imports to aid in execution! I\'ll be testing to confirm!\n\n\\n\\n\n\nI\'m also working on creating a Storybook Library with starter stories, so users have pre-loaded picture books. Each book will have 4-5 pages. I will use the generate_image function to create illustrations for the stories. Every page will have a \"Generate New Illustration\" button.\n\n\n**Implementing New Illustration Features**\n\nI\'m now integrating new features for illustrations! Users will now be able to generate a custom illustration for any page, using `gemini-3-pro-image-preview` via `/api/illustrate`. Even better, users can create custom stories, specifying a topic, age range, art style (like watercolor or collage), and the number of pages. This feature uses `gemini-4-hydrogen` with a structured JSON `responseSchema` to automatically generate a multi-page illustrated storybook with illustrations!\n\n\n\n**Adding Text-to-Speech Functionality**\n\nI\'m now implementing text-to-speech on the server side, specifically at `/api/tts`. The goal is to return WAV audio (base64 encoded), allowing smooth playback through HTML5 `Audio` or the Web Audio API. I\'m building in playback speed controls (0.85x, 1.0x, 1.15x) and comprehensive error feedback to handle potential API quota or key limit issues.\n\n\n**Refining Chatbot Capabilities**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the Story Buddy, enhancing its multi-turn chat experience. I\'m building a chat interface with scrollable threads and conversation history. System instructions will define chatbot roles, dynamically selecting between `gemini-4-carbon`, `gemini-4-argon`, `gemini-4-hydrogen`, and `gemini-3.1-flash-lite` based on task complexity. My goal is a delightful and useful companion for users!\n\n\n**Defining Chatbot Roles**\n\nI\'m now diving deep into the different chatbot roles, assigning distinct personalities and tasks to models. I\'m carefully wiring four models (`gemini-4-hydrogen`, `gemini-4-carbon`, `gemini-4-argon`, and `gemini-3.1-flash-lite`) to specific kid-friendly roles with tailored instructions. The Story Companion is designed for general questions, Deep Wonder Guide tackles complex reasoning, the Plot & Puzzle Architect handles interactive elements, and the Quick Word Helper provides instant assistance. Each will be context-aware of the book and page!\n\n\n**Planning Illustration Batches**\n\nI\'m now planning the initial illustrations. I\'m focusing on \"Phase 1\" and the batch generation. I will generate illustrations for the three starter books, using `generate_image` for covers and hero illustrations. I\'ll focus on warmth, handcrafted feel, and children\'s book style art. Each illustration will fit on the page!\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_18397535904833801198"
