    thinking: "**Analyzing Image Paths**\n\nI\'m thrilled with the generated image paths for those illustrations! Specifically, I\'ve confirmed the precise paths returned: `/src/assets/images/story_lantern_fox_1794665576049.jpg`, `/src/assets/images/story_cloud_whale_1794665577257.jpg`, and another. I\'m focusing on parsing these to ensure consistent naming conventions.\n\n\n**Building Phase 2**\n\nI\'m now meticulously double-checking all the phase two requirements. I\'m focusing on the `metadata.json`, ensuring the name and description are set correctly and that `majorCapabilities` is as expected. I\'m also reviewing the `index.html`, making sure the title and meta descriptions are in sync. Finally, I\'m examining the `package.json` file, with the scripts in mind. I need to make sure the start script is correctly set to `\"start\": \"node server.ts\"`, and I will double-check the Node setup (and typescript support) and view the line contents.\n\n\n**Examining Server Setup**\n\nI\'m now carefully examining the server setup, focusing on `server.ts`. I\'m going to implement an Express server on port 3000, binding to `0.0.0.0`, with Vite middleware in development and static file serving in production. I\'m also preparing to initialize the Gemini client and defining the `/api/tts` endpoint, which will use the Gemini model for text-to-speech. I\'m planning to make sure the environment variables are all set up correctly, with `dotenv`. I\'m starting by viewing the contents of `package.json`, before moving on to setting up `server.ts`.\n\n\n**Implementing API Endpoints**\n\nNow, I\'m diving into the API endpoints. Specifically, I am focusing on the `/api/tts` endpoint, ensuring it correctly handles the input parameters for text-to-speech requests, including `text`, `voiceName`, `readingStyle`, and `ageBand`. I\'m going to leverage `ai.models.generateContent` with the specified configurations and handle the response to extract the audio data. Then, I\'ll move on to crafting the `/api/illustrate` endpoint, making sure I implement the prompt generation logic and validate inputs like `imageSize` and `aspectRatio`.\n\n\n**Developing Illustration Endpoint**\n\nI\'m now building the illustration endpoint. I\'ve configured it to handle requests with optional prompt customization, while explicitly specifying no text in the artwork. I\'m calling `ai.models.generateContent` with image configuration, focusing on aspect ratio and image size, and I\'m omitting `responseMimeType` and `responseSchema` at this stage. I\'m focusing on locating image data from the response and returning the image URL, size, and caption. I need to make sure I iterate through the candidates and parts to properly access the data.\n\n\n**Defining Model Configurations**\n\nI\'m now defining the model configurations! I\'ve mapped the four required models to Story Buddy roles: `gemini-4-hydrogen` for the Story Companion, `gemini-4-carbon` for the Deep Wonder Guide, `gemini-4-argon` for the Adventure Architect, and `gemini-3.1-flash-lite` for the Quick Word Helper. The server is validating allowed model IDs, enforcing tailored system instructions for each, and including context like the story title and page number. It\'ll pass conversation history and return replies. I\'m focusing on error handling.\n\n\n"
